<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) (Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator))",
        "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py> ;
    schema:about "Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2, a PSM-wide period/phase gradient (Lauschke 2013 kinematic waves are only reproduced within ~50 um of the front), 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy, or the mouse somite AP length beyond an order-of-magnitude anchor (~100 um, Gomez et al. 2008)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability",
        "reconstructed_in_script: [Pass 3] 1D anteroposterior excitable chain with juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling and a regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient: arrest front g(F) = g_crit, frozen-phase Mesp2-like switch, 8 stripes with S = 101.7 um vs v_wf T = 102.0 um (CV 0.024), 0 um anterior pulse leak at gamma_F = 1.6 (802 um at 0.8), v_wf / lambda_F / gamma_F sweeps and uniform-FGF ablation (0 stripes)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: [Pass 3] Stiffness -> F-actin tension -> LATS1/2 -> three-state YAP kinetics cascade fitted to the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), E_crit = 12.6 kPa, dynamic Latrunculin A rescue (onset 30.8 min, period 142.5 min), and a 48-cell Dll1-Notch ring synchrony sweep (Kuramoto R 0.27 -> 0.80)",
        "reported_in_source: Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront law S = v_wf T; Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) posterior-high fgf8 mRNA gradient regressing with axis elongation and positioning the determination front; Dupont et al. (2011) YAP/TAZ cytoplasmic on ~0.7 kPa and nuclear on ~40 kPa fibronectin hydrogels under Rho/F-actin control; Wada et al. (2011) stress fibres inhibit LATS1/2",
        "reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction",
        "reported_in_source: Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA",
        "transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with a dorsal chick-embryo somite SEM (Wikimedia 'Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg', filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg) whose px spacing has no um calibration",
        "transfer_boundary: The FGF/Wnt gate acts additively on I_eff (gamma_F (g(F) - 1)) and the determination front is defined by the Hopf margin, which is a reduced reading of Hubaud et al. (2017) Fig. 7 and of the clock-and-wavefront literature, not an equation published in the source paper; the chain is 1D with no cell flow, convergent extension or mediolateral extent",
        "transfer_boundary: The YAP cascade is a lumped ODE keeping both a LATS-dependent branch (Wada 2011) and a LATS-independent tension-driven import branch; Dupont et al. (2011) reported the stiffness response as largely LATS-independent, and the E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin constants are modelling choices, not measured values" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "3. Phase/Delay Oscillators" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Periodic Somites & Segments" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Somite Length S = u·T_clock" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py; output: docs/media/yap_excitable_segmentation_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: eb7a0a2051924df9834d2292bd3eca5cca883f40d58bf2c4618667071ccac50f; artifact_sha256: b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/scout_manifest.json=852a6ed7852f291d..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json=afec7ed9c8b4fd64...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction | Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA | Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront law S = v_wf T; Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) posterior-high fgf8 mRNA gradient regressing with axis elongation and positioning the determination front; Dupont et al. (2011) YAP/TAZ cytoplasmic on ~0.7 kPa and nuclear on ~40 kPa fibronectin hydrogels under Rho/F-actin control; Wada et al. (2011) stress fibres inhibit LATS1/2; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109) | RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability | 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010) | [Pass 3] 1D anteroposterior excitable chain with juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling and a regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient: arrest front g(F) = g_crit, frozen-phase Mesp2-like switch, 8 stripes with S = 101.7 um vs v_wf T = 102.0 um (CV 0.024), 0 um anterior pulse leak at gamma_F = 1.6 (802 um at 0.8), v_wf / lambda_F / gamma_F sweeps and uniform-FGF ablation (0 stripes) | [Pass 3] Stiffness -> F-actin tension -> LATS1/2 -> three-state YAP kinetics cascade fitted to the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), E_crit = 12.6 kPa, dynamic Latrunculin A rescue (onset 30.8 min, period 142.5 min), and a 48-cell Dll1-Notch ring synchrony sweep (Kuramoto R 0.27 -> 0.80); transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with a dorsal chick-embryo somite SEM (Wikimedia 'Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg', filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg) whose px spacing has no um calibration | The FGF/Wnt gate acts additively on I_eff (gamma_F (g(F) - 1)) and the determination front is defined by the Hopf margin, which is a reduced reading of Hubaud et al. (2017) Fig. 7 and of the clock-and-wavefront literature, not an equation published in the source paper; the chain is 1D with no cell flow, convergent extension or mediolateral extent | The YAP cascade is a lumped ODE keeping both a LATS-dependent branch (Wada 2011) and a LATS-independent tension-driven import branch; Dupont et al. (2011) reported the stiffness response as largely LATS-independent, and the E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin constants are modelling choices, not measured values; does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2, a PSM-wide period/phase gradient (Lauschke 2013 kinematic waves are only reproduced within ~50 um of the front), 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy, or the mouse somite AP length beyond an order-of-magnitude anchor (~100 um, Gomez et al. 2008)]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
