<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Each Pass 3 section header and docstring names the law, the source and the Lean theorem it implements (Sections 4b-4d), the math KG registers six equations with lean_locus and code_locus, and the figure panels, measurements and self-test checks are labelled by law. Deductions: the FGF gate form g(F) = F^h/(F_thr^h + F^h) with F_thr = 0.15, h = 4 and gamma_F = 1.6 is traced to no equation or figure of any cited paper (-4); the mechanical constants E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp = 1/12, k_PP = 1/20 and tau_actin = 8 min are declared as module constants without citations (-3); the Kuramoto phase is an atan2 around the fixed point, which is not a protophase correction and is uncited (-1); the ensemble/logistic mismatch at L447-456 is undocumented (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L720–L723: Defect: Hill gate g(F) and its F_thr / h_F defaults are not traced to a published equation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L720-L723>",
        "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L957–L965: Defect: mechanical constants E_50, h_E, A_50, m_L, r0, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin, overexpression factor declared without source citations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L957-L965>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The published FHN fast-slow core, YAP gate and 2D excitable PDE are unchanged and verified (Laws 1-3, L171-604). Pass 3 adds the two missing mechanisms the v2 audit asked for and proves their governing identities in Lean (Theorems 4-6): the regressing exponential Fgf8 gradient (Dubrulle 2001) gating I_eff with an arrest criterion that reproduces S = v_wf T to 0.3% and the analytic front offset to 0.4% (L707-886), and a three-state YAP import/export/phosphorylation cycle whose monotonicity in tension and LATS is proved cross-multiplied (L954-1139). Deductions: the FGF gate gamma_F (g(F) - 1) is additive and phenomenological rather than an Fgf8/Wnt3a/Hes7 circuit, and gamma_F had to be raised from 0.8 to 1.6 for the excitable waves to actually arrest at the front, which is a tuned rather than derived number (-3); the 6-regime benchmark's 200-cell ensemble (L447-453) is computed but never used - the predicted oscillating fraction is a logistic of the deterministic I_eff with a hand-set margin 0.115 and width 0.125 (L451-456), so the r = 0.9976 reflects two fitted constants rather than ensemble dynamics (-3); the cascade keeps a LATS branch that Dupont (2011) found largely dispensable for the stiffness response (disclosed, -1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L447–L456: Defect: 200-cell ensemble osc_mask is computed but pred_frac is a hand-tuned logistic of the deterministic I_eff (margin 0.115, width 0.125); the ensemble only feeds a reporting field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L447-L456>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1218-1352) now returns 11 reference-anchored measurements: the five v2 ones plus stripe spacing S vs v_wf T and the ~100 um mouse somite anchor, the Cooke-Zeeman slope vs T, the cascade RMSE vs the regime table, E_crit vs the Dupont bracket, the LatA onset latency vs one clock period, and the Kuramoto R vs complete synchrony with an uncoupled control; each carries a unit, method and note with the ablation / sweep numbers. Deductions: several new references are analytic or bracket values rather than measured specimen numbers (S vs v_wf T is a self-consistency check of the chain against its own tail-bud period; E_crit's 5.3 kPa 'reference' is a geometric midpoint; the LatA onset reference is an upper bound) (-4); the mouse somite length anchor is an order-of-magnitude value with no digitised Gomez (2008) table vendored (-2); the specimen CV 0.201 is never contrasted with the model CV 0.024 (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
