<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — MorphoEval overall 91.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 post-remediation evaluation of `2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py` (91.8/100, v2 91.7). Both v2 remediation items are closed: the excitable FHN core is now coupled along a 1D anteroposterior axis to an explicit regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient through a Hill gate on I_eff, so that the clock arrests at a moving determination front and freezes a Mesp2-like stripe pattern whose spacing (101.7 um) matches the Cooke-Zeeman law v_wf T (102.0 um) across a 5-point v_wf sweep (slope 144.8 min vs T 145.7 min, r 0.99998), with lambda_F controlling PSM length (407-735 um) but not S, gamma_F controlling whether excitable pulses leak anteriorly (802 um at 0.8, 0 um at the default 1.6) and uniform FGF abolishing the stripes; and nuclear YAP is now produced by a substrate-stiffness -> F-actin -> LATS1/2 -> YAP phosphorylation / import cascade calibrated on the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), predicting E_crit = 12.6 kPa inside the Dupont (2011) 0.7-40 kPa bracket and a dynamic Latrunculin A ignition 30.8 min after F-actin loss, while J_Dll1 became an explicit juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling that synchronises a heterogeneous ring (R 0.27 -> 0.80). Three new Lean 4 theorems (Theorems 4-6) back the new mathematics (6 total, 0 sorrys). The round also surfaced the next layer of defects: the 200-cell ensemble in the 6-regime benchmark is decorative (the predicted fraction is a hand-tuned logistic of I_eff), the vendored specimen is a chick embryo SEM filed as mouse with no um scale, the FGF gate and several mechanical constants are uncited modelling choices, the cascade cannot reproduce the non-monotonic Y-27632 vs high-density pair, and the PSM clock has no phase gradient outside ~50 um of the front. Overall 91.8/100 (faithfulness 91.5, reproducibility 92.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 95, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/yap_excitable_segmentation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py at d58a084, image/png, 1578308 B, 2775×2475 px, artifact_sha256 b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6 (sha256 b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6), spec_fingerprint eb7a0a2051924df9834d2292bd3eca5cca883f40d58bf2c4618667071ccac50f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eb7a0a2051924df9834d2292bd3eca5cca883f40d58bf2c4618667071ccac50f; artifact_sha256: b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/scout_manifest.json=852a6ed7852f291d..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json=afec7ed9c8b4fd64...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction | Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA | Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront law S = v_wf T; Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) posterior-high fgf8 mRNA gradient regressing with axis elongation and positioning the determination front; Dupont et al. (2011) YAP/TAZ cytoplasmic on ~0.7 kPa and nuclear on ~40 kPa fibronectin hydrogels under Rho/F-actin control; Wada et al. (2011) stress fibres inhibit LATS1/2; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109) | RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability | 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010) | [Pass 3] 1D anteroposterior excitable chain with juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling and a regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient: arrest front g(F) = g_crit, frozen-phase Mesp2-like switch, 8 stripes with S = 101.7 um vs v_wf T = 102.0 um (CV 0.024), 0 um anterior pulse leak at gamma_F = 1.6 (802 um at 0.8), v_wf / lambda_F / gamma_F sweeps and uniform-FGF ablation (0 stripes) | [Pass 3] Stiffness -> F-actin tension -> LATS1/2 -> three-state YAP kinetics cascade fitted to the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), E_crit = 12.6 kPa, dynamic Latrunculin A rescue (onset 30.8 min, period 142.5 min), and a 48-cell Dll1-Notch ring synchrony sweep (Kuramoto R 0.27 -> 0.80); transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with a dorsal chick-embryo somite SEM (Wikimedia 'Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg', filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg) whose px spacing has no um calibration | The FGF/Wnt gate acts additively on I_eff (gamma_F (g(F) - 1)) and the determination front is defined by the Hopf margin, which is a reduced reading of Hubaud et al. (2017) Fig. 7 and of the clock-and-wavefront literature, not an equation published in the source paper; the chain is 1D with no cell flow, convergent extension or mediolateral extent | The YAP cascade is a lumped ODE keeping both a LATS-dependent branch (Wada 2011) and a LATS-independent tension-driven import branch; Dupont et al. (2011) reported the stiffness response as largely LATS-independent, and the E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin constants are modelling choices, not measured values; does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2, a PSM-wide period/phase gradient (Lauschke 2013 kinematic waves are only reproduced within ~50 um of the front), 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy, or the mouse somite AP length beyond an order-of-magnitude anchor (~100 um, Gomez et al. 2008)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:447-456 — the 200-cell ensemble (y_samples, j_samples, osc_mask) is computed but `pred_frac` is a logistic of the deterministic I_eff with a hand-set detection margin (0.115) and width (0.125), so the 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9976 reflects two tuned constants rather than ensemble dynamics. Use the ensemble fraction (np.mean(osc_mask), or RK4 on each sampled cell) as the prediction, or derive the margin/width from the ensemble sigma_Y / sigma_J, and report the fit honestly.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:687-701 and 621-684 — the J_max -> Kuramoto R sweep is not strictly monotone (it saturates: 0.802 at J_max = 0.20 vs 0.801 at 0.30, Spearman 0.94) and the phase is an atan2 around the fixed point rather than a protophase-corrected phase; use a Hilbert / protophase estimator, average over several seeds and heterogeneity levels, and compare with Riedel-Kruse (2007) or Hubaud (2017) dissociation-reaggregation synchrony data.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:720-748 — the FGF/Wnt gate g(F) = F^h/(F_thr^h + F^h) with F_thr = 0.15, h = 4 and gamma_F = 1.6 is a phenomenological additive term on I_eff; gamma_F had to be tuned from 0.8 to 1.6 for the excitable pulses to arrest at the front. Replace it with (or calibrate it against) an explicit Fgf8/Wnt3a -> Hes7/Lfng input taken from a cited model, and vendor the Dubrulle (2001) fgf8 gradient profile as a fixture.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:750-886 — the clock is quasi-synchronous across the PSM and only slows within ~50 um of the front (Panel G), so the Lauschke (2013) phase-gradient / kinematic travelling waves are not reproduced. Add a posterior-to-anterior period gradient (e.g. tau_v(x) or I_eff(x) ramp) and measure the wave speed and phase-gradient wavelength against Lauschke et al. (2013) mPSM values.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:957-965 and 1000-1031 — the cascade constants (E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp = 1/12, k_PP = 1/20, tau_actin = 8 min, 2x Yap5SA overexpression) and the per-regime mechanical inputs are uncited modelling assignments, and the tension-only cascade cannot reproduce the non-monotonic Y-27632 (0.30) vs high-density mPSM (0.18) pair (RMSE floor 0.054). Vendor Dupont (2011) / Wada (2011) measured values, add a density / contact-inhibition term, and store the fitted (alpha_T, kappa_LATS, T_L) as a pinned fixture.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json:50-58 and 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:1173-1214 — the vendored SEM is a chick embryo ('Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg') filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg, with no um per px scale, so neither the organism nor the 100 um stripe spacing can be compared with it. Add a correctly named mouse PSM specimen (or relabel as chick and change the organism claim), record a scale, and compare S_model (um) with the specimen in um." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.18e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Parameter expressivity: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every new morphospace parameter is swept and behaves monotonically as claimed: v_wf -> S linearly (5 points, slope 144.8 min = T, r 0.99998), lambda_F -> PSM length (407 / 571 / 735 um vs analytic 410 / 574 / 737) with S unchanged, gamma_F -> anterior pulse leak (802 um at 0.8, 0 um at >= 1.2), uniform FGF -> 0 stripes, E_sub -> Y_nuc monotone with E_crit inside the Dupont bracket, J_max -> Kuramoto R (0.27 -> 0.80, Spearman 0.94), plus the v2 Y_nuc bifurcation sweep and 6-regime suite. New CLI flags --v-wf, --lambda-F and --E-sub expose the two mechanisms. Deductions: the J_max -> R relation is not strictly monotone (it saturates: 0.802 at 0.20 vs 0.801 at 0.30; Spearman 0.94) and the ring uses a tau_v CV fixed at 0.04 (-3); the sweeps are reported as numbers and one scatter panel, without rendered stripe patterns along the v_wf sweep (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seeds (2016) throughout, bitwise determinism asserted for both the 2D PDE and the new 1D chain, a least-squares calibration that is deterministic from fixed initial guesses, --self-test with the Pass 3 checks (stripe count, CV, S vs v_wf T, PSM length vs analytic, ablation, sweep slope, lambda_F invariance, wave arrest vs leak control, cascade RMSE, regime states, E_crit bracket, LatA onset, R monotonicity, 11 measurements with reference values) passing in ~6 s, and the default invocation regenerating the PNG and GIF in ~13 s. Deductions: no requirements lock file is vendored for this slot (-4); the GIF/PNG are not asserted byte-identical across runs (only the model arrays are) (-2); the calibration result depends on scipy.optimize internals and is not pinned by a stored fitted-parameter fixture (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Source and data traceability: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Eight primary sources now carry DOIs in the module docstring, the dataset README, paper_citations.bib and the reference JSON (four added in Pass 3: Cooke & Zeeman 1976, Dubrulle 2001, Wada 2011, Gomez 2008); the specimen and scout manifest remain SHA-256 pinned and verified at runtime (L131-162); the new mechanisms' parameters and regime mechanical inputs live in the reference JSON and are loaded by the script rather than hard-coded, and a pre-existing D_u inconsistency (18 vs 24 um^2/min) between the JSON, the math KG and the code was corrected. Deductions: the regime mechanical inputs (E = 40 kPa for fibronectin-coated dishes, A = 2000 / 150 um^2, rho_actin 0.15, c_ROCK 0.25) are modelling assignments without a per-value source (-3); the specimen filename misstates the organism (-2); the reference JSON is not SHA-pinned (digest recorded, not asserted) (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Panel F still segments both bilateral somite rows of the vendored SEM (8 + 8 somites, 47.14 px, CV 0.201) and Panels G/H now place a generated discrete stripe pattern (8 stripes, S = 101.7 um, CV 0.024) beside it, with the Mesp2-like switch strip, the determination front and the tail bud drawn on the kymograph, so the figure finally shows somite-like periodic clefts emerging from the clock rather than only waves. Deductions: the specimen is a chick embryo SEM (source URL 'Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_ chick_embryo.jpg', reference JSON L55) filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg, and the v2 audit's 'vertebrate' wording hid this - the organism match is a transfer, not a mouse specimen (-6); the specimen spacing is in px with no um calibration, so the 100 um model stripes and the 47 px somites cannot be compared on one scale (-3); the model stripe CV (0.024) is an order of magnitude below the specimen CV (0.201) and the figure does not comment on it (-2); the 1D stripes have no mediolateral shape to compare with the rounded somite blocks (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json L50–L58: Defect: specimen source URL identifies a chick embryo SEM, filed under a 'mouse_psm' filename with no um/px scale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json#L50-L58>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

