<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud et al. (2017) FitzHugh-Nagumo Cubic Fast Nullcline Extrema & Barrier Law" ;
    dct:description "Defines the N-shaped folded cubic nullcline knees at u = +/- 1 that separate monostable excitable quiescence (|u^*| > 1) from autonomous relaxation oscillations (|u^*| < 1) | Variables: u: fast activator (Notch / LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 activity); v: slow negative-feedback recovery variable; f(u) = u - u^3/3: cubic fast nullcline nonlinearity" ;
    dct:source "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171(3):668-682 Fig. 3 & STAR Methods" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L171-L256>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L22-L49> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fhn_cubic_scaled (u : Int) : Int :=
  3 * u - u * u * u
def fhn_cubic_deriv (u : Int) : Int :=
  1 - u * u
theorem hubaud_2017_fhn_cubic_nullcline_extrema :
    fhn_cubic_deriv 1 = 0 ∧
    fhn_cubic_deriv (-1) = 0 ∧
    fhn_cubic_deriv 0 = 1 ∧
    fhn_cubic_scaled 1 - fhn_cubic_scaled (-1) = 4"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "f(u) = u - u^3 / 3,  f'(u) = 1 - u^2 = 0 at u = +/- 1,  Delta_f = f(+1) - f(-1) = 4/3" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.fhn_cubic_deriv" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_fhn_cubic_nullcline_extrema" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud et al. (2017) Supercritical Hopf Stability Boundary vs Quiescent Branch Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the fixed point is unstable (Tr J > 0, autonomous limit cycle) on the middle branch |u^*| < sqrt(1 - epsilon*b) and stable (Tr J < 0, excitable quiescent) on the outer branches |u^*| >= 1 | Variables: u^*: nullcline intersection fixed point; epsilon = tau_u / tau_v: fast-slow timescale ratio (0.08); b: slow recovery damping parameter (0.8)" ;
    dct:source "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171(3):668-682 Figs. 3-4 & STAR Methods" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L204-L380>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L51-L75> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fhn_jacobian_trace (M eps_b u_sq : Int) : Int :=
  M * (1 - u_sq) - eps_b
theorem hubaud_2017_hopf_vs_quiescent_stability (M eps_b : Int)
    (h_pos : 0 < eps_b) (h_fast_slow : eps_b < M) :
    fhn_jacobian_trace M eps_b 0 > 0 ∧
    fhn_jacobian_trace M eps_b 1 < 0"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Tr(tau_u * J(u^*)) = 1 - (u^*)^2 - epsilon * b,  |u_H| = sqrt(1 - epsilon * b)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.fhn_jacobian_trace" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_hopf_vs_quiescent_stability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud et al. (2017) YAP Mechanotransduction Excitability Gating & Latrunculin A Rescue Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that inhibiting nuclear YAP (Latrunculin A, Y-27632 Rockout, soft substrate, Yap1 KO) raises I_eff across the Hopf threshold to ignite autonomous Hes7/Lfng oscillations, whereas Yap5SA locks quiescence | Variables: I_eff: net excitability current; Y_nuc: nuclear YAP translocation fraction [0, 1]; J_Dll1: Notch-Dll1 intercellular coupling input; gamma_YAP: YAP excitability threshold gain" ;
    dct:source "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171(3):668-682 Figs. 4-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L191-L498>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L77-L98> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def yap_effective_current (I_basal J_Dll1 gamma_YAP Y_nuc : Int) : Int :=
  I_basal + J_Dll1 - gamma_YAP * Y_nuc
theorem hubaud_2017_latrunculin_yap_inhibition_rescue
    (I_basal J_Dll1 gamma_YAP Y_high delta_Y : Int) :
    yap_effective_current I_basal J_Dll1 gamma_YAP (Y_high - delta_Y) -
      yap_effective_current I_basal J_Dll1 gamma_YAP Y_high =
      gamma_YAP * delta_Y"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "I_eff(Y_nuc, J_Dll1) = I_basal + J_Dll1 - gamma_YAP * Y_nuc,  Delta I_eff = gamma_YAP * Delta Y_nuc" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.yap_effective_current" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_latrunculin_yap_inhibition_rescue" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) Clock-and-Wavefront Somite Spacing Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that successive arrests of the excitable clock at the regressing FGF/Wnt determination front freeze the phase exactly S = v_wf T apart, the spacing of the Mesp2-like somite stripes measured in simulate_ap_wavefront_arrest and the slope of the v_wf sweep | Variables: x_wf: anteroposterior position of the determination front; v_wf: axis-elongation / wavefront regression speed (um/min); T: segmentation-clock period (min); n: clock cycle index" ;
    dct:source "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) J Theor Biol 58(2):455-476, DOI 10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2; Hubaud et al. (2017) Cell 171:668-682 Fig. 7" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L704-L952>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L110-L129> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wavefront_position (x_wf0 v_wf t : Int) : Int :=
  x_wf0 + v_wf * t
theorem hubaud_2017_clock_wavefront_somite_spacing (x_wf0 v_wf t0 T n : Int) :
    wavefront_position x_wf0 v_wf (t0 + (n + 1) * T) -
      wavefront_position x_wf0 v_wf (t0 + n * T) = v_wf * T"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x_wf(t) = x_wf0 + v_wf * t,  x_wf(t0 + (n+1) T) - x_wf(t0 + n T) = v_wf * T" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.wavefront_position" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_clock_wavefront_somite_spacing" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Dubrulle et al. (2001) FGF/Wnt-Gated Wavefront Arrest Criterion" ;
    dct:description "Defines the determination front as the locus where FGF/Wnt loss exceeds the Hopf margin (wavefront_gate_threshold, g_crit) and proves that the front regresses at v_wf regardless of lambda_F, so lambda_F sets PSM length but not somite spacing (lambda_F sweep in evaluate_wavefront_speed_sweep) | Variables: F: Fgf8/Wnt3a signal (posterior-high exponential, decay length lambda_F); g(F): Hill gate; gamma_F: FGF/Wnt excitability gain; I_post: tail-bud excitability current; I_H: lower Hopf current; d: fixed decay distance from tail bud to front" ;
    dct:source "Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106(2):219-232, DOI 10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8; Hubaud et al. (2017) Cell 171:668-682" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L707-L748>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L131-L160> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fgf_gated_current (I_post gamma_F g_max g : Int) : Int :=
  I_post - gamma_F * (g_max - g)
theorem hubaud_2017_fgf_wavefront_arrest_criterion
    (I_post gamma_F g_max g I_H x_tb0 v_wf t dt d : Int) :
    (fgf_gated_current I_post gamma_F g_max g < I_H ↔
      I_post - I_H < gamma_F * (g_max - g)) ∧
    ((wavefront_position x_tb0 v_wf (t + dt) - d) -
      (wavefront_position x_tb0 v_wf t - d) = v_wf * dt)"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F(x,t) = min(1, exp(-(x_tb(t) - x)/lambda_F)),  g(F) = F^h/(F_thr^h + F^h),  I_eff = I_post - gamma_F (g_max - g);  arrested <=> gamma_F (g_max - g) > I_post - I_H" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.fgf_gated_current" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_fgf_wavefront_arrest_criterion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Dupont et al. (2011) / Wada et al. (2011) YAP Mechanotransduction Nuclear-Fraction Monotonicity Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves (cross-multiplied, division-free) that the steady-state nuclear YAP fraction rises with tension-driven import and falls with LATS phosphorylation, so softer substrates, smaller spreading area, Latrunculin A and Y-27632 all lower Y_nuc toward Y_crit and ignite the clock (calibrate_yap_mechanotransduction, evaluate_substrate_stiffness_sweep, simulate_latrunculin_yap_kinetics) | Variables: T: F-actin/stress-fibre tension index in [0,1] from substrate stiffness E_sub (kPa), spreading area A_cell (um^2), F-actin content rho_actin (Latrunculin A) and ROCK contractility c_ROCK (Y-27632); L(T): LATS1/2 activity; r_n: tension-driven nuclear import/export ratio; r_p: LATS phosphorylation/dephosphorylation ratio; Y_n: nuclear YAP fraction feeding Law 3" ;
    dct:source "Dupont et al. (2011) Nature 474(7350):179-183, DOI 10.1038/nature10137; Wada et al. (2011) Development 138(18):3907-3914, DOI 10.1242/dev.070987; Hubaud et al. (2017) Cell 171:668-682 Figs. 4-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L954-L1139>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean#L162-L199> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def yap_nuclear_denominator (r_n r_p : Int) : Int :=
  1 + r_n + r_p
theorem hubaud_2017_yap_mechanotransduction_monotonicity
    (r_n1 r_n2 r_n r_p r_p1 r_p2 : Int)
    (h_rp : 0 ≤ r_p) (h_lt : r_n1 < r_n2) (h_rn : 0 < r_n) (h_p : r_p1 < r_p2) :
    r_n1 * yap_nuclear_denominator r_n2 r_p < r_n2 * yap_nuclear_denominator r_n1 r_p ∧
    r_n * yap_nuclear_denominator r_n r_p1 < r_n * yap_nuclear_denominator r_n r_p2"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T(E,A) = [E^hE/(E50^hE + E^hE)] [A/(A50 + A)] rho_actin c_ROCK,  L(T) = 1/(1 + (T/T_L)^m),  Y_n = r_n/(1 + r_n + r_p),  r_n = r0 (1 + alpha_T T),  r_p = kappa_LATS L(T)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.070987> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo Somite Clock Gated by YAP Mechanotransduction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.yap_nuclear_denominator" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_027.hubaud_2017_yap_mechanotransduction_monotonicity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

